From: Prabhsimran Singh <prabhsimrans@nvidia.com>
Subject: ggml-cuda: CUDA graph cache keys, replay updates and eviction knobs

- Key cached graph executables by graph identity and structural shape, so
  allocator reuse cannot select an executable for a different shape.
- Refresh node parameters when a cached graph is replayed, so per-stream
  state pointers that change every call keep the graph resident.
- GGML_CUDA_GRAPH_EVICT_AFTER_MS, read when a backend is created, sets how
  long an idle graph is kept (default 10 s; 0 keeps graphs resident).

Upstream: the shape key is the follow-up requested in
ggml-org/llama.cpp#28243 and the eviction knobs are a small candidate; replay
updates are NeMo-specific.

